# Shorup News — Cursor project rules

You are working on **Shorup News**, a Bangladesh-focused news intelligence product: multi-source headline clusters, perspective/bias signals, rumor flags, blindspot detection, and **AI claim verification**. Installable **PWA**; UI is English + Bangla where the app already uses both.

**Detailed rules** live in `.cursor/rules/` (`shorup-news.mdc` always applies; `backend.mdc` / `frontend.mdc` / `supabase.mdc` when editing those trees). Maintainer guide: `docs/CURSOR_RULES.md`.

## Architecture

- `backend/` — Python 3.11+, FastAPI, async SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL (+ **pgvector** / FTS for verified claims), optional **Redis** + **Celery** (ingest + verification queues), RSS ingestion (`app/services/rss_ingestion.py`), Groq/Gemini via `app/services/ai_client.py`; source seed in `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py`; `POST /api/v1/ingest` + `npm run ingest:backend`
- `frontend/` — Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, optional Supabase auth (`src/lib/supabase.ts`, `database.types.ts`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up`)
- `supabase/` — migrations for profiles, Pro subscriptions, bKash records, user dossiers/alerts (news + verified claims stay in backend Postgres)
- Root scripts: `npm run dev:frontend`, `dev:backend`, `ingest:backend`, **`worker:backend`**, **`worker:beat`**, **`worker:verification`**, **`stack:up`** / **`stack:down`** (`docker-compose.yml`: Postgres pgvector, Redis, API, Celery worker, **beat** for scheduled RSS)
- **Production releases**: `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` (deploy order, migrations, rollback, checklist)
- **Claim verification**: `POST /api/v1/verify` (guardrailed submit), `/api/v1/verifications/*` (jobs, SSE/WS, list/search/detail); UI `/verify`, `/verify/[slug]`, `/verify/database` via `src/lib/verifications.ts`
- **Public sources**: `GET /api/v1/sources` (optional `custom_only`) + `GET /api/v1/articles?source_id=` — admin-added RSS and per-source article reads (no admin key); optional helper `fetchCustomSourcesFeed` in `api.ts`
- **Admin ops (internal)**: backend `GET /api/v1/admin/overview` (includes **`ingest_schedule`**) + **`GET/PATCH /api/v1/admin/ingest-schedule`** (`app_settings`, migration `003_app_settings.sql`; Celery beat tick when `REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`) + RSS source add/remove (`admin.py` → `admin_stats` / `admin_sources` / **`ingest_schedule`**; DELETE purges articles/orphan clusters then soft-disables seed or deletes custom; `sources.disabled`, migration `002_sources_disabled.sql`); frontend **`admin.shorup.news`** in production (`admin-host.ts`, local `/admin`) gated by legacy cookie or **Supabase admin**; tabbed **`AdminDashboardPanel`** (overview, sources/ingest, system, **Users**, issues) + `GET /api/admin/overview` → `{ overview, apiHealthy }`; legacy **`shorup_admin`** cookie still required for sources/ingest/**ingest-schedule**/users proxies (overview allows Supabase admin — see `frontend.mdc`)
- **PWA deploy resilience**: `chunk-load-error.ts` — one-shot reload on chunk failures (`error.tsx` / `global-error.tsx`; dev SW unregister in `layout.tsx`); see `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`
- **Monitoring (optional)**: Sentry on backend (`app/core/sentry_init.py`) and frontend (`@sentry/nextjs`, `instrumentation.ts`); ingest cron pings via `app/services/ops_alerts.py` (Healthchecks.io + Telegram when env is set)

## Conventions

### Backend
- Thin routes in `app/api/`; logic in `app/services/`; schemas in `app/schemas/`; models in `app/models/`
- Async for I/O; config in `app/core/config.py`; API prefix `/api/v1`; optional `INGEST_API_KEY` / `ADMIN_API_KEY`; Redis-backed rate limits when `REDIS_URL` is set; never commit secrets

### Frontend
- Pages under `frontend/src/app/`; components in `src/components/`; route errors in `app/error.tsx`, `app/global-error.tsx`, and `app/not-found.tsx`; segment `loading.tsx` on story/verify detail
- Fetch via `api.ts` + `api-resilience.ts`, `stories.ts` (API + `demo-data.ts` fallback, `fromApi` + `ApiDegradedBanner`; cluster blurbs from RSS via **`source-digest.ts`**); articles may include RSS `image_url` (`ArticleImage` on browse/rumors); cluster detail articles carry `source_name` / `bias_score` for perspective, blindspot (`blindspot.ts`, `/blindspot`), and partiality (`partiality.ts`); story detail **`StoryShareBar`**, **`StoryTabs`** (Coverage / Compare / Perspectives) + **`StoryCoverageDetails`**; verification via `verifications.ts` (`lookupVerifiedClaim` for slug detail)
- Pro tier: `subscription-features.ts` (matrix, taglines, `PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS` — analytics only; news open to all), `subscription-entitlement.ts` + `subscription-access.ts` (Supabase `subscriptions` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`), `subscription-plans.ts` (pricing); **`/pro`** (**Plans**) + **`PaywallModal`** (`featureId` for Pro-only analytics)
- Home: static `/` + `HomeStoryGridClient` hydrates from `GET /api/feed/top` (`getTopStories`, ETag/`feed-etag.ts`); story `/story/[slug]` via **`StoryDetailPanel`** + `GET /api/story/[slug]` (`client-story-cache.ts`); **`HOME_TOP_STORIES_LIMIT`** from `subscription-features.ts`; full archive on **`/browse`** for everyone
- Server components for feeds; client components for interactive UI — wrap fragile client trees in `ClientErrorBoundary`
- Reads degrade to demo when the API is down; writes (verify submit, admin) must surface real failures

## Product vocabulary

- **Cluster / headline clash** — Same story, different framings
- **Perspective** — neutral, establishment, opposition, international (spectrum tabs on **`StoryArticleFeed`**)
- **Bias meter** — Scored lean for a source or cluster
- **Rumor badge** — Unverified or speculative coverage
- **Blindspot** — Establishment or opposition press missing while the other side dominates (`blindspot.ts`; `/blindspot` feed)
- **Partiality** — Any perspective bucket still empty in a multi-source cluster (`partiality.ts`; banners/teasers on story detail and feed cards)
- **Verified claim** — Completed fact-check with verdict + analysis (`/verify/[slug]`, backend `verified_claims`)
- **Shorup Pro** — All users get full news (home highlights + `/browse`); Pro unlocks analytics extras in `PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS` (`subscription-features.ts`; compare on `/pro`)

## Quality bar

- Match existing layout and naming; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
